{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/70477-hunting-changelings","id":70477,"title":"Hunting Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-12T04:24:05-08:00","id":70477,"title":"Hunting Changelings","content":"I know it says in the Changeling book that most Changelings blend pretty well, but the Hunter books do mention, albeit not often in comparison to the other types of supernatural, that Hunters sometimes go after Changelings. What I'm a little confused about is<br /> <br /> 1) how Changelings get on the Hunters radar: most of what they do doesn't really hit the hunter Richter scale, rarely needing to kill, and usually not in a flagrantly supernatural way. And unless they have like a cult or something, I don't really see pledges being super-obvious, especially given the semi-natural appearance of how they're fulfilled? The books talk a lot about Hunters seeing Changelings as dream-eaters, and while I can see people being upset about that, again, how would they know unless they themselves experience it? In my experience people rarely talk about their dreams, and never to the point of being able to discern some kind of trend.<br /> <br /> 2) even if the Hunters do somehow work out there's something funky going on, how could they trace it back to the Changeling themselves? Rarely does the Changeling need to be in close physical proximity: if they're invading dreams they most likely have a pledge or in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> I'm obviously ruling out high Wyrd/Mantle Changelings here, since they're kind of more the exception than the rule, at least to the point where it's that obvious.<br /> <br /> How do you see this unfolding, or how have you run it in your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T06:01:48-08:00","id":70520,"title":"","content":"Compacts and Conspiracies. I think unless you're hunting the odd rogue monster the major splats really require a long-term approach with a lot of careful research by quite a lot of people. And that really requires a level of commitment and motivation that hopefully individual hunter cells aren't going to have.<br /> <br /> That said, there are plenty of Changeling groups who are great targets for Hunters: the Scarecrow Ministry and the Miami Court of Winter spring to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:41:33-08:00","id":70691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/70477-hunting-changelings#post70477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) how Changelings get on the Hunters radar: most of what they do doesn't really hit the hunter Richter scale, rarely needing to kill, and usually not in a flagrantly supernatural way. And unless they have like a cult or something, I don't really see pledges being super-obvious, especially given the semi-natural appearance of how they're fulfilled? The books talk a lot about Hunters seeing Changelings as dream-eaters, and while I can see people being upset about that, again, how would they know unless they themselves experience it? In my experience people rarely talk about their dreams, and never to the point of being able to discern some kind of trend.</div> </div> </div> </div>The keyword is &quot;most&quot;. Sometimes Changelings do kill, sometimes Changelings trick someone into a horrible Pledge, but one where the victim can still ask the local Union for help and look for a way out. Sometimes the True Fae screw up and the family see the abduction take place.<br /> <br /> <br /> Other times, well Hunters aren't always trying to kill the monsters. A little research will tell you that faeries like to make deals, and yeah that's dangerous but Hunters do dangerous stuff all the time. It's better than dealing with a Demon. Hunters might try to find a faerie who can sell info like the names of all the local Vampires or hire a faerie to break a witch's curse. If hunters know about Goblin Markets - magic weapons, magic powers, and they want you to come shopping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/70477-hunting-changelings#post70477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) even if the Hunters do somehow work out there's something funky going on, how could they trace it back to the Changeling themselves? Rarely does the Changeling need to be in close physical proximity: if they're invading dreams they most likely have a pledge or in the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Hunters might have an Endowment that lets them see through the Mask, others might have that ability naturally and become a hunter because of what they can see. The rest of the time, lots of surveillance and looking for people who fit the psychological profile or staking out all those places granny says people used to tell stories about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, faeries are probably more of a specalist job than Werewolves or Witches.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Click Dream Catchers in my sig. A full PDF about faerie hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T19:42:20-08:00","id":70985,"title":"","content":"Read the story in the Hunter's Recongnition Guide.Some Changelings might still be indebted to their Keepers. They might be sending Humans off to Arcadia to save their skins. That's where Hunters would come in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}